# npc_and_faction_relations.md.backup

This sanitized outline documents the NPC and Faction Relations systems in a setting-agnostic format.

## Faction Framework

- Maintain a configurable list of major factions stored in data assets.
- Track standing values per faction for each player profile.
- Surface helper utilities to query allies, neutrals, and hostiles at runtime.

## Reputation Flow

- Mutate reputation values through additive or absolute updates depending on event context.
- Major events can consume helper functions such as `applySectorOutcome()` to distribute rewards and penalties without exposing narrative specifics.
- Reputation influences vendor inventories, dialogue availability, quest hooks, and AI behavior flags.

## NPC Integration

- Dialogue nodes reference faction thresholds when selecting conversation branches.
- NPC behavior scripts consult reputation values to toggle recruitable or hostile states.
- Persistence is delegated to the Save System so relationship changes survive between sessions.

## Implementation Guidelines

- Keep faction metadata in external configuration; avoid embedding world lore in source-controlled code.
- Validate that localization files provide neutral phrasing so sanitized exports remain spoiler-free.
- Record balancing adjustments in design logs instead of system documentation.
